-- title:
--   Base change of modular function field generated by j and j_N
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field equipped with an algebra structure over $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $N$ be a nonzero natural number. Write $jq \in \mathbb{Q}((q))$ for the Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the image in $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ of the integral power series `jNum`, i.e. the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-invariant, and let `qExpand ℚ d` be the ring endomorphism of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ substituting $q \mapsto q^{d}$ (transport of the Hahn-series exponents along multiplication by $d$ on $\mathbb{Z}$). The field `modularFunctionFieldFull N` is the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}((q))/\mathbb{Q}$ generated by all `qExpand ℚ d jq` with $d$ a nonzero divisor of $N$, and its base change `laurentBaseChange L (modularFunctionFieldFull N)` is the intermediate field of $L((q))/L$ generated by the image of that set under the coefficientwise embedding `coeffEmb L` induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$. The assertion is that, inside this base-changed field, the $L$-intermediate field generated by just the two elements `coeffEmb L jq` and `coeffEmb L (qExpand ℚ N jq)` — each taken with its membership in the base change — is all of it, i.e. equals $\top$.
--
--   This is the $L$-rational form of the classical statement that the function field of $X_0(N)$ is generated by $j$ and $j_N = j(q^N)$; it supplies the generation half used to compare or extend embeddings of that field by their values on these two elements alone, and says nothing about the degree of the extension or the modular polynomial $\Phi_N$. It is invoked throughout the analysis of places and Hecke divisors on the characteristic-$p$ models of the modular curve.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_adjoin_jBar_jNBar_eq_top.lean

